I'll refactor the code to move all view management, state, layout operations, and API work from Desktop.vue to the views store, eliminating duplication.

## Analysis

**Issues identified:**
1. Desktop.vue handles panel events (add, remove, layout changes) that duplicate views store logic
2. Layout persistence and restoration logic split between both files
3. Panel error handling and synchronization in Desktop should be coordinated through the store
4. App-to-panel sync logic is duplicated

**Solution:**
- Move all desktop API interactions to views store actions
- Desktop.vue becomes a thin UI layer that listens to store changes
- All layout, panel, and app management goes through the store

---

## Changes

| File | Changes |
|------|---------|
| src/store/views.js | Add desktop event handling, panel management, layout change detection |
| src/components/desktop/Desktop.vue | Remove duplicate logic, simplify to UI layer only |

